 Why globals: TwinCAT requires a constructor-style initializer when an
 FB's FB_init has user-defined inputs (FB_StationFill / FB_StationInspect
 take ModeRef + AlarmHandler + DataLogger). The compiler ALSO refuses to
 resolve those init args against locally-declared FB instances in the
 same VAR_INST block ("The initial value for a VAR_INST variable may not
 use local variables"). Globals are the only references the compiler
 will accept in a VAR_INST initializer, so the test fixtures live here.

